#!/bin/sh
# Wrapper autour du binaire next-wakeup de kindle-dash (renommé next-wakeup.bin).
# dash.sh l'appelle ainsi : next-wakeup --schedule="..." --timezone="Europe/Paris"
# On calcule le prochain réveil pour chaque horaire (celui passé en argument + EXTRA_SCHEDULES,
# séparés par ";") et on renvoie le plus proche.
DIR="$(dirname "$0")"
TZ_OPT="--timezone=Europe/Paris"
SCHED=""
for a in "$@"; do
  case "$a" in
    --timezone=*) TZ_OPT="$a" ;;
    --schedule=*) SCHED="${a#--schedule=}" ;;
  esac
done
ALL="$SCHED"
[ -n "$EXTRA_SCHEDULES" ] && ALL="$ALL;$EXTRA_SCHEDULES"
best=""
IFS=';'
for s in $ALL; do
  [ -z "$s" ] && continue
  v=$("$DIR/next-wakeup.bin" --schedule="$s" "$TZ_OPT" 2>/dev/null)
  case $v in '' | *[!0-9]*) continue ;; esac
  if [ -z "$best" ] || [ "$v" -lt "$best" ]; then best=$v; fi
done
unset IFS
[ -z "$best" ] && best=600
echo "$best"
